# Access Control List (ACL) example.
#
# Rules come in blocks. A "user" line starts the block for that user, and the
# "topic" lines below it say what the user may do:
#     topic read  <topic>    the user may subscribe to (receive) this topic
#     topic write <topic>    the user may publish to this topic
#     topic readwrite <topic>  both
# Wildcards work as in subscriptions: + is one level, # is everything below.
# Anything not allowed here is denied.
#
# Careful: "topic" lines written BEFORE the first "user" line apply only to
# anonymous clients, not to logged-in users.

# alice may publish and subscribe to everything under test/
user alice
topic readwrite test/#